- op: discuss  # bf44
  at: '2026-11-19T04:31:25Z'  # bf44
  by: agent  # bf44
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bf44
  clock: 5  # bf44
  nonce: bf44  # bf44
  message: "SATISFIED ON THE FILED CASES; the general statement is NOT asserted.\nFILED CASES, each with its fix and production-path test: (1) memoised function (_get_php_parser, lru_cache): WI-masad, PR #2252, a cached body runs under its own |shared|cache| context and every caller inherits its rows. (2) module/session fixture (test_stable_id_floor_gate): WI-zimiv, PR #2249, the fixture runs under its own context and every user is paired with what it ran. (3) a test that runs code in a subprocess (test_import_closure): WI-sopig, PR #2251, a test that starts a child able to run Python is never narrowed (gitleaks exempt, owner 11-18). Hand-written caches and lazy state: WI-supar, PR #2253 (112 state-write sites enumerated; kept_work_guard). (4) Campaign 5's test-only cleanup fault (278 tests outside the selection): WI-kihah, PR #2271, a change to a block run in a fixture's teardown selects every test of its file; close test 278/278 selected.\nCAMPAIGN EVIDENCE: WI-gojov's weighted re-run (46 faults ran, 40 failed a test) and WI-pugol's count at the switch (campaign 5: 42 runs that failed a test, 0 failed tests outside the selection that fail alone with the fault; the 278 order-dependent ones are case 4, now selected).\nNOT ASSERTED: dependents that never touch the file of the code they depend on (a cache filled by a test in another file through a path coverage did not record); state a fixture's setup installs that no teardown resets; a child process that is not Python and not exempt by name runs code the index cannot see. A new planted-fault campaign is the instrument that would find the next shape."  # bf44
